       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg daily is three times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses that high raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **3 mg**, if a decimal or unit slip changed the dose.\n\nIf 30 mg is intentional, tell me and add a short rationale. I can enter it with a note saying the dose was confirmed by you as the attending. Pharmacy will probably flag it for verification.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
